I was really worried that
Nina's plants would die,

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.507
and it would make me very sad

00:04:44.507 --> 00:04:47.309
because Nina would be very
said, but these look great.

00:04:47.309 --> 00:04:49.908
So it's good to be back.
Shaking off my headache.

00:04:49.908 --> 00:04:52.009
Wanted to share one final parenting tip

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:54.604
that we've picked up that helped.

00:04:54.604 --> 00:04:57.361
The first one I talked
about in a previous video,

00:04:57.361 --> 00:05:00.794
we did one present per
person, and they knew.

00:05:00.794 --> 00:05:03.878
And actually they all knew they wanted

00:05:03.878 --> 00:05:05.614
the Harry Potter wand before even going,

00:05:05.614 --> 00:05:07.597
so they didn't even ask.

00:05:07.597 --> 00:05:09.241
- [Nina] Yeah, they didn't ask.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:10.726
- The whole time, right?

00:05:10.726 --> 00:05:12.085
The whole time they didn't say I want this

00:05:12.085 --> 00:05:14.231
and I want this and I want this.

00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:15.498
That was really good.

00:05:15.498 --> 00:05:18.766
I made that up, kind of four years ago,

00:05:18.766 --> 00:05:22.173
and I think every year we just
made it more and more clear

00:05:22.173 --> 00:05:24.850
earlier and earlier, and
that part was fantastic.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:28.436
We didn't get bothered at all
about wanting different gifts

00:05:28.436 --> 00:05:31.573
so that's amazing, like we got
to start preparing for that

00:05:31.573 --> 00:05:33.843
for next year, one gift.

00:05:33.843 --> 00:05:35.449
The other thing that we did that was new

00:05:35.449 --> 00:05:39.655
that we made up on the spot
this year was time-outs.

00:05:39.655 --> 00:05:42.539
So what I did was, so in our
family we don't do spanking.

00:05:42.539 --> 00:05:45.624
We do time-outs, so you get
time-outs for misbehaving.

00:05:45.624 --> 00:05:48.809
Any time they misbehaved or complained,

00:05:48.809 --> 00:05:51.310
we gave them a minute time-out.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.091
To get rid of a minute, they had to do

00:05:53.091 --> 00:05:55.230
a good deed for somebody else.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.536
It was a good, like we
started that like midway

00:05:57.536 --> 00:06:00.593
through the vacation, I feel
like we're going to start

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:04.760
it sooner next year and
maybe ratchet up the points

00:06:07.515 --> 00:06:11.365
a little faster, but I
think it worked out well.

00:06:11.365 --> 00:06:13.706
They hated getting the time-outs,

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:16.994
and then they were
looking ways for trying--

00:06:16.994 --> 00:06:19.185
- Trying to do good deeds.

00:06:19.185 --> 00:06:20.666
- To do good deeds for people.

00:06:20.666 --> 00:06:22.233
- Even before this time-out started.

00:06:22.233 --> 00:06:23.843
- Yeah, so if they had a good
deed before they had minutes,

00:06:23.843 --> 00:06:25.861
they got negative one minute.
I think that worked out well.

00:06:25.861 --> 00:06:27.841
We got to try that next time.

00:06:27.841 --> 00:06:30.187
Anyway, parenting tips from
Evan and Nina (laughs).

00:06:30.187 --> 00:06:32.601
